BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting NORMA 
 (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocation: Netherlands-based a
 rts-sector activity. No city or region restriction stated.\nAward: Maximum
  EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may not exceed EUR 150\,000
  and the applicant organisation's annual budget may not exceed EUR 500\,00
 0. At least 25 percent of the project budget must come from audience or bo
 x-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 wage norms of EUR 139 
 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No application fee.\nDuration: 
 Single project\, typically a production or concert series. Final report du
 e within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/
 norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuurloket-digitall-implementatiebijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultuurloket DigitALL: Implementation Contribution (Imple
 mentatiebijdrage\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:A one-off 2026 call letting Dutch cultural institutions reuse a
 nd adapt digital technology that other institutions have already built and
  published in the open DigitALL Toolkit\, for example translation software
  shared between theatres or a streaming platform adapted for a new venue. 
 Grants run up to EUR 30\,000 and cover technical modification\, integratio
 n\, production and deployment costs.\n\nOrganisation: Cultuurloket DigitAL
 L\nLocation: Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city o
 r region restriction.\nAward: Up to EUR 30\,000. Covers technical modifica
 tion\, system integration\, production and deployment costs. Hardware purc
 hase alone is ineligible unless clearly essential to the public experience
 . No stated co-financing percentage. No application fee.\nDuration: Not sp
 ecified\; scoped to a single implementation.\n\nMore: https://cultuurloket
 digitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuurloketdigitall.nl/implementatiebijdrage/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands and the Caribbean parts of the Kingdom. No city or reg
 ion restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-international-vouchers-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261027
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261028
SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count).\n\nOrganisation: St
 imuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within E
 urope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per tr
 ip\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouch
 ers?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stroom-den-haag-pro-art-projects-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261025
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stroom Den Haag: PRO Art Projects
DESCRIPTION:Stroom Den Haag's PRO Art Projects scheme contributes to the co
 sts of realising a contemporary art project. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, cura
 tors\, critics\, publicists\, partnerships and organisations.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Stroom Den Haag\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicant
 s from outside The Hague (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes pl
 ace in The Hague or otherwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hagu
 e artists must be registered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).\nAward:
  Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project\, up to EUR 20\,000 per applicant per cal
 endar year. Requests above EUR 5\,000 require at least 30 percent co-finan
 cing of the total budget from third parties. Artist fees\, production and 
 communication costs are eligible\; Stroom endorses the kunstenaarshonorari
 um.nl fee guideline. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\; the gr
 ant remains valid for up to two years after the decision meeting\, with 80
  percent paid upfront and 20 percent on the final report\n\nMore: https://
 www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-projects?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stroom.nl/en/stroom-for-artists/financial-support/pro-art-p
 rojects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands. Open to applicants from outside The Hague
  (apply with a CV) as long as the project takes place in The Hague or othe
 rwise benefits art and artists in The Hague\; Hague artists must be regist
 ered in the Stroom database (Mijn Stroom).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stichting-stokroos-seed-grant-autumn-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Stokroos: Seed Grant\, Autumn 2026 round
DESCRIPTION:The Stokroos Seed Grant supports early-practice visual artists\
 , designers and craft practitioners in the Netherlands with an unrestricte
 d budget for a self-defined plan: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\, EUR 7\,500 
 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives. The plan must start at least 10 we
 eks after submission\, last no longer than a year\, and can take place any
 where in the world.\n\nOrganisation: Stichting Stokroos\nLocation: Applica
 nts must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (including its Ca
 ribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the funded plan itself 
 can take place anywhere in the world.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 for individuals\,
  EUR 7\,500 for duos\, EUR 10\,000 for collectives\, as an unrestricted co
 ntribution to a self-defined plan. No application fee.\nDuration: Funded p
 lan starts at least 10 weeks after submission and lasts up to one year\n\n
 More: https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://stokroos.nl/en/grant-rules/seed-en/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must live and work in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (i
 ncluding its Caribbean parts) or Suriname for at least one year\; the fund
 ed plan itself can take place anywhere in the world.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cifnl-videotage-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Industries Fund NL: Residency Videotage 2027 (Ho
 ng Kong)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL offers one residency at Videota
 ge\, the Hong Kong media art institute (est. 1986) known for critical work
  on XR\, AI\, blockchain and video games.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Indust
 ries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie)\, with Videotage\nLoc
 ation: Hong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in 
 the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sin
 t Maarten and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business regist
 er (KvK).\nAward: One residency grant: EUR 5\,000 for a two-month work per
 iod or EUR 6\,500 for three months\, covering travel\, insurance\, living 
 expenses\, compensation for time invested\, and material and transport cos
 ts. Housing\, work space\, Videotage guidance and production costs are pai
 d by the Fund directly to Videotage on top of the grant\; accommodation is
  arranged by Videotage. No application fee.\nDuration: 23 March to 18 May 
 2027 (two months) or 23 March to 15 June 2027 (three months)\; state your 
 preferred period. Research period plus a concluding public presentation ev
 ent for Videotage's Hong Kong network.\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfo
 nds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-videotage?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Hong Kong (Videotage premises). Only for applicants established in
  the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Si
 nt Maarten and registered with a Kingdom of the Netherlands business regis
 ter (KvK).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-embassy-brussels-cultural-support-nov-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Embassy in Brussels: Open Call for Cultural P
 roject Support
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Embassy in Brussels runs several open calls per
  year subsidising Dutch-Belgian artistic and cultural projects in Belgium 
 that strengthen the Netherlands' cultural profile and promote cooperation 
 between the two countries.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of the Kingdom of the 
 Netherlands in Brussels\nLocation: Belgium. Applicants must be professiona
 l creators\, organisations\, institutions or legal entities in Belgium wit
 h a company registration number\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dut
 ch-Belgian projects.\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 per project.\nDuration: Roll
 ing open calls with multiple deadlines per year\; next deadlines 3 Novembe
 r 2026 and 18 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlemba
 ssy-brussels-open-call-for-support?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlembassy-brussels-open-call-for-suppo
 rt?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Belgium. Applicants must be professional creators\, organisations\
 , institutions or legal entities in Belgium with a company registration nu
 mber\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dutch-Belgian projects.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:amsterdam-light-festival-open-call-edition-16@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T160829Z
DTSTART:20261207T222900Z
DTEND:20261207T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Amsterdam Light Festival Edition 16 Open Call (
 light art\, EUR 4\,000 artist fee plus production costs)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 07 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nAmsterdam Light Festival in
 vites light art concepts for its 16th edition (2027-2028)\, presented alon
 g and on the canals of Amsterdam. WHO: creatives from all over the world\,
  individually or as a team\; multiple submissions are allowed and existing
  work may be considered.\n\nOrganisation: Amsterdam Light Festival\nLocati
 on: Amsterdam\, the Netherlands. Main call open to creatives worldwide\; t
 he Open Call X Amarte strand is for Netherlands-based makers new to light 
 art. Works are shown on the Amsterdam canals.\nAward: EUR 4\,000 artist fe
 e per selected maker\, with the costs of making the artwork and travel cov
 ered by the festival. Open Call X Amarte: EUR 4\,000 artist fee plus a EUR
  20\,000 production budget. No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: Festi
 val runs 25 November 2027 to 16 January 2028 (about 7 weeks).\n\nMore: htt
 ps://amsterdamlightfestival.com/en/open-call?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://amsterdamlightfestival.com/en/open-call?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, the Netherlands. Main call open to creatives worldwide
 \; the Open Call X Amarte strand is for Netherlands-based makers new to li
 ght art. Works are shown on the Amsterdam canals.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
